eer viewer (deletion pass), and convert agent.agent/agent.chat in the agent repo (they still build __benchPlatform).\",\n    \"tags\": \"bench-collapse\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786401039404\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Bench collapse complete in both repos: dev IDE, peer viewer, and the agent app (chat/askrow/describebtn/agentloop/agentprompt/memory) all run stock; /dev/, /peer/ and /agent/ verified headless with zero console errors.\",\n    \"detail\": \"Library ready-ordering rule: a library control defines its global in me.ready and lists its own library deps as child divs; api.js activation guarantees children's readys before the parent's, transitively — so consumers gate their init on me.ready (readyP = new Promise(res => me.ready = res)). Remaining vestige: dev.code.set_module_flag (newbound_core-rooted, needs host rebuild to delete — left for a platform-side cleanup on a session without the overlay initializer entanglement). Known follow-up: /agent/ serving requires runtime/agent scaffold (publishapp output) — clone-fresh instances need the _APPS/agent copy, same as the disposable recipe's metaidentity seeding.\",\n    \"tags\": \"bench-collapse\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786403684763\n  }\n]\n","patch_id":"p14","time":1786405099436}]},"id":"khxopo19fb8616d67h1_patches","readers":[],"time":1786405099436,"username":"system","writers":[]}